<topic id="index">
  <title>DITA Bootstrap PDF</title>
  <shortdesc>Two plug-ins for
    <xref href="http://www.dita-ot.org" format="html" scope="external">DITA Open Toolkit</xref> that extend the default
    PDF output with a
    <xref
      href="https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3"
      format="html"
      scope="external"
    >Bootstrap 5.3</xref> templating and components.
  </shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Bootstrap 5.3</indexterm>
        <indexterm>DITA</indexterm>
        <indexterm>installing</indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>
    <section>
      <title>Installing</title>
      <p>Use the <cmdname>dita</cmdname> command to add the plug-ins to your DITA Open Toolkit installation:</p>
    </section>
     <accordion>
        <accordion-item open="yes">
        <title>DITA-OT 3.5 and newer</title>
          <ol>  
            <li>
              <p><b>Optional:</b> install the specialization plug-in to add support for new DITA elements that
               generate Bootstrap components:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.dtd</codeblock>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>For PDF generation, install the PDF plug-in, and the PDF theme plug-in as shown:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.pdf
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.pdf.theme</codeblock>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>To add syntax highlighting using the Bootstrap color scheme, install the Prism.js plug-in if required:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >install</parmname> fox.jason.prismjs</codeblock>
            </li>
          </ol>
      </accordion-item>
      <accordion-item>
        <title>DITA-OT 3.3 and newer</title>
          <ol>  
            <li>
              <p><b>Optional:</b> install the specialization plug-in to add support for new DITA elements that
               generate Bootstrap components:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.dtd</codeblock>
          </li>
          <li>
          <p>For PDF generation, install the PDF plug-in, and add the PDF theme plug-in as shown:
          </p>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.pdf
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>--install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.pdf.theme</codeblock>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>To add syntax highlighting using the bootstrap color scheme, install the Prism.js plug-in if required:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> fox.jason.prismjs</codeblock>
            </li>
          </ol>
      </accordion-item>
      <accordion-item>
        <title>DITA-OT 3.2 and older</title>
          <ol>  
            <li>
              <p><b>Optional:</b> install the specialization plug-in to add support for new DITA elements that
               generate Bootstrap components:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/dita-bootstrap/dita-bootstrap.dtd/archive/develop.zip</codeblock>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>For PDF generation, install the PDF plug-in, and add the PDF theme plug-in as shown:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/dita-bootstrap/dita-bootstrap.pdf/archive/master.zip
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/dita-bootstrap/dita-bootstrap.pdf.theme/archive/master.zip</codeblock>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>To add syntax highlighting using the bootstrap color scheme, install the Prism.js plug-in if required:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/jason-fox/fox.jason.prismjs/archive/master.zip</codeblock>
            </li>
          </ol>   
      </accordion-item>
    </accordion>
    <section>
      <title>Using</title>
      <p>Specify the <option>pdf-bootstrap</option> format when building output with the <cmdname>dita</cmdname>
        command:</p>
      <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
        >--input</parmname>=path/to/your.ditamap <parmname>--format</parmname>=pdf-bootstrap</codeblock>

       <p>If using DITA-Bootstrap specialization, ensure that the <codeph
        >*.dita</codeph> files are using the following <codeph>DOCTYPE</codeph> declaration:</p>
       <codeblock
        outputclass="language-xml"
      >&lt;!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//DITA Bootstrap//DTD DITA Bootstrap Topic//EN" "bootstrap-topic.dtd"&gt;</codeblock>
        
    </section>
    <section>
      <title>Bootswatch themes</title>
      <indexterm><parmname>--bootstrap.theme</parmname></indexterm>
      <p>PDFs can be generated to align with the themes Bootstrap themes available at
        <xref href="https://bootswatch.com/" format="html" scope="external">Bootswatch</xref>.
        To override the default appearance with a Bootswatch theme, pass a theme name to the <cmdname
        >dita</cmdname> command via the <parmname>--bootstrap.theme</parmname> parameter:
      </p>

      <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>--input</parmname>=<filepath
        >path/to/your.ditamap</filepath> \
     <parmname>--format</parmname>=<option>pdf-bootstrap</option> \
     <parmname>--bootstrap.theme</parmname>=<option>&lt;theme-name&gt;</option></codeblock>
     <p><b outputclass="h4">Parameters</b></p>
     <parml otherprops="cols(4)">
        <plentry>
          <pt>
            <parmname>--bootstrap.theme</parmname>
          </pt>
          <pd>
            Defines the style of the PDF  - <option>default</option> applies default Bootstrap styling.
          </pd>
        </plentry>
      </parml>

